# Interpreter artifacts, not source. Studies 016-018 already carry the same two
# rules locally; this lifts them to the root so a test run anywhere in the tree
# cannot add bytecode to a commit.
#
# Nothing here ignores a retained study artifact. Study harnesses that pin
# bytecode caches do so by digesting them at run time and comparing against
# compile() -- they never commit a .pyc, and a committed one would describe an
# interpreter rather than the source it was built from.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
